# What the FUNCTION does not need. Bundle size is a hard 225 MB limit and
# exceeding it fails the deployment, so this is correctness, not tidiness.
#
# Kept, because the function imports them: api/, web/, pipeline/lib/, config/
# (pipeline/lib/taxonomy.py reads config/taxonomy.yaml, reached from
# api/staffing.py), and public/ for the static explorer.
tests/
eval/
docs/
knowledge/
db/
commands/
.claude-plugin/
.drive-cache/
.github/
00-master/
01-workflows/
02-curriculum/
03-instructors/
04-programs/
05-operations/
06-analysis/
*.md
!README.md
# EVERY top-level pipeline script, by glob rather than by name. This was eight
# hand-written entries and five scripts added since were simply not in it —
# gen_index, gen_landing_stats, gen_workflow_owners, query and
# check_no_payroll_committed were all being uploaded. A hand-written list of
# what to exclude means a new file is INCLUDED by default, which is the same
# permissive-default shape as property_scopes and §A.7b instance 8.
#
# pipeline/lib/ is deliberately NOT matched: api/staffing.py reaches
# config/taxonomy.yaml through pipeline/lib/taxonomy.py, and `pipeline/*.py`
# does not match `pipeline/lib/*.py`.
# tests/test_documented_constraints_are_enforced.py fails if one slips back in.
pipeline/*.py
# ...but keep the package marker explicitly. `pipeline/*.py` matches
# __init__.py too. The deploy works without it because namespace packages
# carry `from pipeline.lib import taxonomy` — but "it happens to work" is not
# how the import path that reads taxonomy.yaml should be held together.
!pipeline/__init__.py
